  "facts": {
    "prout-named": "The King has spoken of Wendell Prout, his grain clerk of twenty years, and the letter Prout wrote him a week ago asking for an audience about irregularities in the Royal Granary Roll, which he has put off until after the Assembly."
  },
  "background": [
    "This is the same evening as the King's Road. What happened at the crossroads and Garrow's bridge is in what happened just before this scene, and that wins: how the fights went, whether Corporal Haskett is on her feet, what the player found (heron pennies, Garrow's ledger), and how Guardsman Wren stands with them. Wren has brought them up from the gate; Fitch has taken Tansy and the cushions round to the palace's back door."
  ],
