        "closing": "The King goes down for the toasts with crumbs on his waistcoat, turning at the door to say one small true thing about the player (how they take their tea, what they did on the bridge). A footman shows them up to a small room high under the palace roof, with a fire, a green cushion on the chair, and the city's lamps going out one by one beyond the window. End on the player falling asleep in the King's palace. Don't narrate the morning.",
        "result": "good",
