      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Shown the door",
        "description": "Last resort. The player has made a scene the King can't overlook (steel drawn or a blow struck in his parlour, the King threatened, his letters snatched and read aloud to mock him, the Marshal insulted to his face), and Holt has had them put out of the palace into the night by the guards. The King won't send for them again, and the story ends here.",
        "closing": "The palace's side door shuts behind them. The bunting, the cold, the city's lamps going out. Land on the player alone in the street; don't narrate beyond it.",
        "result": "bad",
        "exitKind": "leave",
